<!--
  MFC PlotJuggler layout — SHARED SCHEMA (aircraft-agnostic, sim + real flight).

  All curves are keyed under the fixed root "/uav". Both telemetry sources are
  rewritten into this schema before reaching PlotJuggler (pj_json_relay.py
  normalize_obj: root -> "uav", STAB_MFC -> MFC_STAB, GUIDANCE_MFC ->
  MFC_GUIDANCE, GUIDANCE_MFC_ACC2ATT/ACC2ATT -> MFC_ACC2ATT):

    SITL (./sim.sh):  NPS scope emitter (nps_scope.c) — ground truth (TRUTH) +
                      firmware-registered vars at full decimated sim rate,
                      normalized and forwarded by sim_anton.py, which writes the
                      SAME packets to sim_logs/mfc_sim_<TS>.csv.
    Real flight:      server.ml UDP/JSON (port 9870) through pj_json_relay.py,
                      which normalizes by default.

  One UDP-Server instance on port 9870, protocol JSON, timestamp field
  "timestamp".

  WHICH TABS FILL ON WHICH FEED — the two feeds do not carry the same branches,
  so tabs are named for what they can actually show:
    * MFC_RPY / MFC_XYZ / ACCEL2ATT / WLS  — both feeds (the controller
      publishes these to the scope AND over ivy).
    * Estim (EST/*)  — both feeds. In flight there is no scope, so
      pj_json_relay.py's FIELD_ALIAS projects ROTORCRAFT_FP into EST/* (fixed-
      point unscaled, ENU->NED) to fill it.
    * "States (sim truth)" (TRUTH/*) — SIM ONLY. JSBSim ground truth has no
      real-flight counterpart (short of OptiTrack).
    * SPvMEAS — mixed: EST + MFC curves draw on both feeds, TRUTH and SP/* only
      in sim.

  UNITS: every angle in this schema is RADIANS. The scope used to emit TRUTH/EST
  in degrees while the controller branches were radians, which made MFC curves
  look flat next to truth on the shared SPvMEAS axes; nps_scope.c and
  nps_scope_state.c now emit the firmware's native radians.
-->
